{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-field-scalar-products","title":"def:smooth-field-scalar-products","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":2573,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:smooth-field-scalar-products","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:smooth-field-scalar-products","line":4327,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Smooth Field of Scalar Products]\n\\label{def:smooth-field-scalar-products}\n\n\\uses{lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear}\n\n\n\n\nLet $\\pi\\colon V\\to B$ be a smooth real vector bundle. A \\emph{smooth field of\nscalar products} is a family of bilinear forms $g_b$ on $V_b$ such that\n\\begin{enumerate}[label=(\\alph*)]\n\\item $g_b$ is symmetric;\n\\item for every nonzero $v\\in V_b$, some $w\\in V_b$ satisfies $g_b(v,w)\\ne0$;\n\\item $b\\mapsto g_b$ is a smooth section of the bundle of bilinear forms on $V$.\n\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Smooth Field of Scalar Products] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a736d6f6f74682d6669656c642d7363616c61722d70726f6475637473\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear\">↗ lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi \\colon V\\to B$\">$\\pi \\colon V\\to B$</span> be a smooth real vector bundle. A <em>smooth field of scalar products</em> is a family of bilinear forms <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_b$\">$g_b$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V_b$\">$V_b$</span> such that <ol><li><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_b$\">$g_b$</span> is symmetric; </p></li><li><p>for every nonzero <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in V_b$\">$v\\in V_b$</span>, some <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$w\\in V_b$\">$w\\in V_b$</span> satisfies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g_b(v,w)\\ne 0$\">$g_b(v,w)\\ne 0$</span>; </p></li><li><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$b\\mapsto g_b$\">$b\\mapsto g_b$</span> is a smooth section of the bundle of bilinear forms on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V$\">$V$</span>. </p></li></ol> ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#cor:scalar-product-signature-sum","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear","title":"lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear","label":"lem:nondegenerate-symmetric-bilinear"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product","title":"lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product","label":"lem:pseudo-metric-fibre-scalar-product"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth","title":"lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth","label":"lem:pseudo-metric-pairing-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-riemannian-metric","title":"def:pseudo-riemannian-metric","label":"def:pseudo-riemannian-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:local-nondegenerate-family","title":"de